  "q": "<p>Your research assistant helps users analyze academic papers over extended conversations. </p><p>User testing reveals a recurring issue: </p><ul><li>after conversations exceed 60K tokens, </li><li>users ask follow-up questions requiring precise numerical details from papers discussed earlier—sample sizes, </li><li>exact p-values, </li><li>specific inclusion criteria. </li></ul><p>Your current approach summarizes paper discussions after 8 turns to stay within context limits. </p><p>Users report that responses to these precision-dependent questions are often hedged or inaccurate. </p><p>What's the most effective architectural change?</p>",
